<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Suwar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1472">1472</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Şehsuvar Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suvar">Suwar</a> was a ruler of the Dulkadirids, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> on the frontier between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. With Ottoman encouragement he rebelled against the Mamluks in the late 1460s and defeated several Mamluk armies. He was finally captured and executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> in 1472, and his brother was installed in his place.</p></div>
